# This file is documentation, not a template. Nothing copies it any more.
#
# render-env.sh generates two env files on every deploy, from this repository's
# Actions secrets plus the public settings in env.public:
#
#   .env          Caddy loads it: the public settings and the secrets below
#                 that backend.env.map does not claim.
#   .env.backend  the backend loads it: the ones it does, each renamed to the
#                 config key the API answers to.
#
# Two files because env_file is all-or-nothing — one would hand the TLS proxy
# the secret that mints click sessions. Editing either on the box works until
# the next deploy overwrites it; change the value in Settings > Secrets and
# variables > Actions instead, and redeploy.
#
# What each secret is for is written here because nothing else can tell you:
# Actions secrets are write-only, so a name is all the GitHub UI ever shows.
#
# Adding one Caddy reads needs no code change at all — create it in the UI and
# it is on the box next deploy. One the API reads needs a line in
# backend.env.map naming the config key it becomes, and nothing else.
#
# Non-secret settings are NOT here — API_DOMAIN and FRONTEND_ORIGIN live in
# env.public, and BACKEND_IMAGE, CADDY_IMAGE, POLL_INTERVAL and
# POLL_RETENTION_DAYS are defaulted by docker-compose.yaml.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the secrets

# Cloudflare API token Caddy uses for the ACME DNS-01 challenge. Create at
# dash.cloudflare.com > My Profile > API Tokens > Create Token > Custom:
#   Permissions: Zone / DNS / Edit  and  Zone / Zone / Read
#   Zone Resources: Include / Specific zone / clickplanet.lol
# Scope it to the one zone, not All Zones.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# Salts the per-sender chat tag (the 6 hex characters beside a name in chat).
# Generate once with `openssl rand -hex 16` and then leave it alone: changing it
# renames every sender at the same time, and an empty value makes the API
# generate a new one on every restart.
CHAT_TAG_SALT=

# Signs the session tokens the Click RPC requires. Generate once with
# `openssl rand -hex 32`. Rotating it is cheap — every client mints again on its
# next click — but it cannot be left empty: the mint and the click check each
# derive a signer from it, so the stack refuses to start rather than run with
# two of them.
SESSION_SECRET=

# Secret key of the Turnstile widget, from dash.cloudflare.com > Turnstile >
# your widget > Settings. Its sitekey is the public half and belongs in the
# frontend build as VITE_TURNSTILE_SITEKEY — do not swap the two. The widget's
# allowed domains must list FRONTEND_ORIGIN's host, and must NOT list localhost
# for a production widget.
TURNSTILE_SECRET=

# ------------------------------------------------------- not on the box, ever

# VPS_HOST, VPS_USER and VPS_SSH_KEY are Actions secrets too, but they drive the
# deploy rather than the app, and render-env.sh excludes them by name. The ssh
# key especially must never be written into a file a container can read.
